{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames","title":"prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":250,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:partial-frame-extension]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pushforward-smooth]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existence-orthonormal-frames]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pullback-immersion-metric]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames","line":444,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Existence of Adapted Orthonormal Frames]\n\\label{prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames}\n\\uses{def:riemannian-metric, lem:partial-frame-extension, lem:pushforward-smooth, lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian, prop:existence-orthonormal-frames, lem:pullback-immersion-metric}\n\\dcref{ch2:2.14}\n\nIf $(\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$ has no boundary and $M\\subseteq\\widetilde M$ is an embedded smooth submanifold with or without boundary, then for every $p\\in M$ some ambient neighborhood of $p$ has a smooth orthonormal frame whose first $\\dim M$ members are tangent to $M$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\nFor a vector bundle $V\\to B$, a local $k$-frame means $k$ smooth sections linearly independent in every fibre (not necessarily spanning). For an immersion, adapted frames live in the ambient pullback bundle of Lemma \\ref{lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian}.","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Existence of Adapted Orthonormal Frames] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a616461707465642d6f7274686f6e6f726d616c2d6672616d6573\"></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-metric\">↗ def:riemannian-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apartial-frame-extension\">↗ lem:partial-frame-extension</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apushforward-smooth\">↗ lem:pushforward-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian\">↗ lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aexistence-orthonormal-frames\">↗ prop:existence-orthonormal-frames</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apullback-immersion-metric\">↗ lem:pullback-immersion-metric</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.14</span></span><p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$\">$(\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$</span> has no boundary and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M\\subseteq \\widetilde M$\">$M\\subseteq \\widetilde M$</span> is an embedded smooth submanifold with or without boundary, then for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> some ambient neighborhood of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> has a smooth orthonormal frame whose first <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\dim M$\">$\\dim M$</span> members are tangent to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span>.  <p></p>For a vector bundle <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V\\to B$\">$V\\to B$</span>, a local <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$k$\">$k$</span>-frame means <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$k$\">$k$</span> smooth sections linearly independent in every fibre (not necessarily spanning). For an immersion, adapted frames live in the ambient pullback bundle of Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a616d6269656e742d74616e67656e742d62756e646c652d7269656d616e6e69616e\">5</a>.","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:spheres","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:ordered-linear-extension","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","label":"def:riemannian-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:partial-frame-extension","title":"lem:partial-frame-extension","label":"lem:partial-frame-extension"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pushforward-smooth","title":"lem:pushforward-smooth","label":"lem:pushforward-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian","title":"lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian","label":"lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existence-orthonormal-frames","title":"prop:existence-orthonormal-frames","label":"prop:existence-orthonormal-frames"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pullback-immersion-metric","title":"lem:pullback-immersion-metric","label":"lem:pullback-immersion-metric"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#exer:gram-schmidt-adapted-frame","title":"exer:gram-schmidt-adapted-frame","label":"exer:gram-schmidt-adapted-frame"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter4#ex:tangential-connection-submanifold","title":"ex:tangential-connection-submanifold","label":"ex:tangential-connection-submanifold"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter5#prop:tangential-covariant-derivative-projection","title":"prop:tangential-covariant-derivative-projection","label":"prop:tangential-covariant-derivative-projection"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames","title":"prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[Existence of Adapted Orthonormal Frames]\n\\label{prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames}\n\\uses{def:riemannian-metric, lem:partial-frame-extension, lem:pushforward-smooth, lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian, prop:existence-orthonormal-frames, lem:pullback-immersion-metric}\n\\dcref{ch2:2.14}\n\nIf $(\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$ has no boundary and $M\\subseteq\\widetilde M$ is an embedded smooth submanifold with or without boundary, then for every $p\\in M$ some ambient neighborhood of $p$ has a smooth orthonormal frame whose first $\\dim M$ members are tangent to $M$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\nFor a vector bundle $V\\to B$, a local $k$-frame means $k$ smooth sections linearly independent in every fibre (not necessarily spanning). For an immersion, adapted frames live in the ambient pullback bundle of Lemma \\ref{lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian}.","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:partial-frame-extension","title":"lem:partial-frame-extension","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pushforward-smooth","title":"lem:pushforward-smooth","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian","title":"lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existence-orthonormal-frames","title":"prop:existence-orthonormal-frames","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pullback-immersion-metric","title":"lem:pullback-immersion-metric","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}